The evidence is consistent. Search's container fails to start and cycles through Failed, BackOff, and Killing events, so this is a pod-level crash loop rather than memory pressure. I'm ready to write up the findings.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT metric, count(*) n, round(avg(value),2) avg_v, min(value) mn, max(value) mx FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name='search' AND metric IN ('k8s.container.ready','k8s.container.restarts') GROUP BY metric",
          "claim": "Search container is never ready in the abnormal window; restarts climb from 3 to 6 per pod."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT left(time::VARCHAR,19) t, regexp_extract(message, '\"reason\":\"([^\"]+)\"', 1) reason FROM abnormal_logs WHERE message ILIKE '%search-77745d5c76-fq4hb%' ORDER BY time",
          "claim": "Search pod events cycle through Failed, BackOff and Killing from 00:17:53, a crash loop rather than a memory event."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name IN ('search','geo','rate') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Search emits no spans during the abnormal window, and its callees geo and rate receive no calls at all."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_http_response_status_code>=500 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) s5xx, round(avg(duration)/1e6,3) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name IN ('search.Search/Nearby','HTTP /hotels') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Frontend's search.Search/Nearby calls fail in about 0.04 ms, and 673 of 678 HTTP /hotels requests return 5xx."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

